# Why this shape: which requirement constrains a part is already in the SysML
# model, in the `satisfy` link. Repeating it here was duplicating the model.
# Anchoring on the part means a new requirement on an already-mapped part
# needs no new mapping entry.
#
# This file stays YAML and stays in git on purpose. FREQ-3 asks for a mapping
# that is human-readable and can be placed under version control -- it is
# design intent and belongs in review. The append-only EVIDENCE log is the
# thing that wants a database; the two are not the same store.
version: 2

